#op: bind
A minor version accepts every value its predecessor accepts at every path. A
bound, a narrower kind or a smaller disjunction rejects values the predecessor
accepted. A field the predecessor admitted only through `...` is the same case
(see also issue #47): it may already hold any value, so declaring it with a type
narrows it.
-- lineage.cue --
name: "ship"
schemas: {
	"0": {
		"0": {
			schema: {
				n: int
			}
		}
		"1": {
			schema: {
				n: int & >=0
			}
		}
	}
}
-- out/json --
{
  "diagnostics": [
    {
      "code": "E0215",
      "severity": "error",
      "headline": "n in schema 0.1 is now uint, which does not accept every value of the prior int",
      "path": [
        "schemas",
        "0",
        "1",
        "schema",
        "n"
      ],
      "address": {
        "field": [
          "n"
        ],
        "kind": "schemaField",
        "version": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      "primary": {
        "file": "lineage.cue",
        "line": 11,
        "col": 5,
        "offset": 100,
        "origin": "user"
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "label": "schema 0.1 is declared as a minor version of 0.0, so every instance of schema 0.0 must be an instance of it (compatibility rule value-narrowed)"
